(2) Ketentuan tentang P2TP2A akan diatur lebih lanjut dalam Peraturan Bupati.  42 ( 1)

translated_text:
Article 11
(1) The implementation of protection for victims is carried out in an integrated manner within the framework of P2TP2A;
(2) Provisions regarding P2TP2A will be further regulated in a Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 12
Bentuk-bentuk pelayanan terhadap korban yang diselenggarankan oleh P2TP2A  meliputi:
a. pelayanan medis berupa perawatan dan pemulihan kondisi fisik yang  dilakukan oleh tenaga medis dan paramedis;
b. pelayanan medicolegal merupakan bentuk layanan medis untuk kepentingan  pembuktian di bidang hukum;
c. pertolongan psikososial pertama pada korban dilakukan untuk identifikasi  terjadinya kekerasan dan traumatis yang dialami korban;
d. pelayanan hukum untuk membantu korban dalam menjalani proses  peradilan;
e. pendampingan korban kekerasan yang dilakukan oleh orang atau lembaga  kompeten yang mempunyai keahlian untuk melakukan konseling, terapi dan  advokasi guna penguatan dan pemulihan korban kekerasan dan telah  bekerjasama dengan P2TP2A; dan
f. pelayanankemandirian ekonomi berupa layanan untuk pelatihan ketrampilan  dan memberikan akses ekonomi agar korban dapat mandiri.
(2) Mekanisme pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (l), diselenggarakan  menurut Standar Operasional Prosedur (SOP) dan diatur lebih lanjut dengan  peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 12
Forms of services for victims organized by P2TP2A include:
a. medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for the purpose of evidence in the legal field;
c. first psychosocial assistance to victims is conducted to identify the occurrence of violence and trauma experienced by victims;
d. legal services to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process;
e. accompaniment of violence victims carried out by competent persons or institutions that have expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of violence victims and have cooperated with P2TP2A; and
f. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.
(2) The service mechanism as referred to in paragraph (1), is organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) and is further regulated by a Regent Regulation.

text:
BAB VII
PERAN SERTA MASYARAKAT
Pasal16 (1) Masyarakat berperan serta dalam perlindungan anak dan perernpuan korban  kekerasan secara perorangan rnaupun kelornpok.
(2) Peran serta rnasyarakat sebagairnana dirnaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan oleh  perseorangan, lembaga perlindungan anak, lernbaga kesejahteraan social,  organisasi kernasyarakatan, lernbaga pendidikan, media rnassa, dan dunia  usaha.
(3) Peran serta rnasyarakat dalarn penyelenggaraan perlindungan anak dan  • perernpuan korban kekerasan sebagairnana dirnaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan  dengan cara :
a. Mernberikan inforrnasi rnelalui sosialisasi dan edukasi;
b. Mernberikan rnasukan dalarn perurnusan kebijakan yang terkait  perlindungan anak dan perernpuan korban kekerasan;
c. Melaporkan kepada pihak berwenang jika terjadi pelanggaran hak anak dan  perernpuan korban kekerasan;
d. Berperan aktif dalarn proses rehabilitasi dan reintegrasi sosial bagi anak dan  perernpuan korban kekerasan;
e. Melakukan pernantauan, pengawasan, dan ikut bertanggungjawab terhadap  penyelenggaraan perlindungan anak dan perempuan korban kekerasan;
f. Berperan aktif dengan rnenghilangkan pelabelan negatif terhadap anak dan  perernpuan korban kekerasan; dan
g. Mernberikan ruang kepada anak dan perernpuan korban kekerasan untuk  dapat berpartisipasi dan rnenyampaikan pendapat.
(4) Peran organisasi kernasyarakatan dan lernbaga pendidikan sebagairnana  dirnaksud pada ayat (2) dilakukan dengan cara rnengambil langkah yang  diperlukan sesuai tugas, fungsi, dan kewenangan rnasing-rnasing untuk  rnernbantu penyelenggaraan anak dan perernpuan korban kekerasan.
(5) Peran media masa sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dilakukan melalui  penyebarluasan informasi dan materi edukasi yang bermanfaat dari aspek sosial,  budaya, pendidikan, agama, dan kesehatan anak dan perempuan korban  kekerasan dengan memperhatikan kepentingan anak dan perempun korban  kekerasan.
(6) Peran dunia usaha sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dilakukan melalui :  a. Kebijakan perusahaan yang prespektif anak dan perempuan korban  kekerasan;
b. Produk yang ditujukan untuk anak dan perempuan korban kekerasan harus  aman bagi anak dan perempuan korban kekerasan;
c. Berkontribusi dalam pemenuhan hak anak dan perempuan korban  kekerasan melalui tanggung jawab sosial perusahaan.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 16 (1) The community participates in the protection of children and women victims of violence individually or in groups.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by individuals, child protection institutions, social welfare institutions, community organizations, educational institutions, mass media, and the business sector.
(3) Community participation in the implementation of protection for children and women victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by:
a. Providing information through socialization and education;
b. Providing input in the formulation of policies related to the protection of children and women victims of violence;
c. Reporting to the authorities if violations of the rights of children and women victims of violence occur;
d. Playing an active role in the process of rehabilitation and social reintegration for children and women victims of violence;
e. Conducting monitoring, supervision, and sharing responsibility for the implementation of protection for children and women victims of violence;
f. Playing an active role by eliminating negative labeling of children and women victims of violence; and
g. Providing space for children and women victims of violence to be able to participate and express their opinions.
(4) The role of community organizations and educational institutions as referred to in paragraph (2) is carried out by taking necessary steps in accordance with their respective duties, functions, and authorities to assist in the implementation of protection for children and women victims of violence.
(5) The role of mass media as referred to in paragraph (2) is carried out through the dissemination of information and educational materials that are beneficial from the social, cultural, educational, religious, and health aspects of children and women victims of violence by taking into account the interests of children and women victims of violence.
(6) The role of the business sector as referred to in paragraph (2) is carried out through:
a. Company policies that have a perspective on children and women victims of violence;
b. Products intended for children and women victims of violence must be safe for children and women victims of violence;
c. Contributing to the fulfillment of the rights of children and women victims of violence through corporate social responsibility.

text:
BAB VIII
PEMBINAAN DAN PENGAWASAN
Pasal 17
(1) Pemerintah Daerah wajib melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan  • penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
(2) Pembinaan dan pengawasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:  a. Pedoman dan standar pemulihan;
b. Bimbingan teknis dan pelatihan;
c. Penyediaan fasilitas;
d. Pemantauan; dan
e. Evaluasi.
(3) Pembinaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dalam rangka mewujudkan  tujuan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan sesuai standar  pelayanan minimal;
(4) Pengawasan terhadap pelaksanaan Peraturan Daerah ini dilakukan oleh  Pemerintah Daerah dan/ atau masyarakat sesuai ketentuan peraturan  perundang-undangan yang berlaku.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VIII
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 17
(1) Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
(2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. Guidelines and standards for recovery;
b. Technical guidance and training;
c. Provision of facilities;
d. Monitoring; and
e. Evaluation.
(3) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) is in order to realize the objectives of protection for women and children victims of violence in accordance with minimum service standards;
(4) Supervision of the implementation of this Regional Regulation is conducted by the Regional Government and/or the community in accordance with the provisions of applicable laws and regulations.

text:
BABIX
LARANGAN
Pasal 20
( 1) Setiap orang dilarang :
a. memper!akukan anak dan perempuan secara diskriminatif yang  mengakibatkan anak dan perempun mengalami kerugian, baik materiil  maupun moriil sehingga menghambat fungsi sosialnya; atau
b. memperlakukan anak dan perempuan penyandang disabilitas secara  diskrimininatif.
(2) Setiap orang dilarang menempatkan, membiarkan, melibatkan, menyuruh  melibatkan anak dan perempuan dalam situasi dan perlakuan salah dan  penelantaran;
(3) Setiap orang dilarang menempatkan, membiarkan, melakukan, menyuruh  melakukan, atau turut serta melakukan kekerasan terhadap anak dan  perempuan;
(4) Setiap orang dilarang melakukan kekerasan atau ancaman kekerasan  memaksa anak dan perempuan melakukan peresetubuhan dengannya atau  orang lain;
(5) Setiap orang dilarang melakukan kekerasan atau ancaman kekerasan,  memaksa, melakukan tipu muslihat, melakukan serangkaian kebohongan,  atau membujuk anak dan perempuan untuk melakukan atau membiarkan  dilakukan perbuatan cabul;
(6) Setiap orang dilarang menempatkan, membiarkan, melakukan, menyuruh  melakukan, atau turut serta melakukan penculikan, penjualan da/atau  perdagangan anak dan perempuan;
(7) Setiap orang dilarang menghalang-halangi anak dan perempuan untuk  menikmati budayanya sendiri, mengakui dan melaksanakan ajaran agamanya  dan/atau menggunakan bahasanya sendiri tanpa mengabaikan akses  pembangunan masyarakat dan budaya;
(8) Setiap orang dilarang merekrut atau memperalat anak dan perempuan untuk  kepentingan militer dan/atau lainnya dan membiarkan anak dan perempuan  tanpa perlindungan jiwa;
(9) Setiap orang dilarang menempatkan, membiarkan, melakukan, menyuruh  melakukan, atau turut melakukan eksploitasi secara ekonomi dan/atau  seksual terhadap anak dan perempuan;
(10) Setiap orang dilarang dengan sengaja menempatkan, membiarkan,  melibatkan, menyuruh melibatkan anak dan perempuan dalam  penyalahgunaan, serta produksi dan distribusi narkotika dan/atau  psikotropika;
(11) Setiap orang dilarang dengan sengaja menempatkan, membiarkan,  melibatkan, menyuruh melibatkan anak dan perempuan dalam  penyalahgunaan, serta produksi dan distribusi alkohol dan adaktif lainnya.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IX
PROHIBITIONS
Article 20
(1) Every person is prohibited from:
a. treating children and women in a discriminatory manner that results in children and women experiencing losses, whether material or moral, thereby hindering their social function; or
b. treating children and women with disabilities in a discriminatory manner.
(2) Every person is prohibited from placing, allowing, involving, ordering the involvement of children and women in situations and treatment of abuse and neglect;
(3) Every person is prohibited from placing, allowing, committing, ordering the commission of, or participating in committing violence against children and women;
(4) Every person is prohibited from committing violence or threat of violence to force children and women to engage in sexual intercourse with him or another person;
(5) Every person is prohibited from committing violence or threat of violence, coercion, committing deceit, committing a series of lies, or persuading children and women to commit or allow the commission of obscene acts;
(6) Every person is prohibited from placing, allowing, committing, ordering the commission of, or participating in committing kidnapping, sale and/or trafficking of children and women;
(7) Every person is prohibited from obstructing children and women from enjoying their own culture, acknowledging and practicing their religious teachings and/or using their own language without neglecting access to community and cultural development;
(8) Every person is prohibited from recruiting or exploiting children and women for military and/or other interests and leaving children and women without protection of their lives;
(9) Every person is prohibited from placing, allowing, committing, ordering the commission of, or participating in committing economic and/or sexual exploitation of children and women;
(10) Every person is prohibited from intentionally placing, allowing, involving, ordering the involvement of children and women in the abuse, as well as production and distribution of narcotics and/or psychotropic substances;
(11) Every person is prohibited from intentionally placing, allowing, involving, ordering the involvement of children and women in the abuse, as well as production and distribution of alcohol and other addictive substances.

